+          <span class="question-text">How can I tell if a cat is happy?</span>
+          <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
+        </button>
+        <div class="details" id="answer-4" hidden>
+          <div class="details-inner">
+            <p>Happy cats usually show relaxed body language: soft eyes, a gently upright tail, calm grooming, and interest in play or attention. Slow blinking and choosing to sit near you are also common signs of trust.</p>
+          </div>
+        </div>
+      </div>
+
+      <div class="example">
+        <button class="question" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="answer-5">
+          <span class="question-text">Why do cats chirp at birds or windows?</span>
+          <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
+        </button>
+        <div class="details" id="answer-5" hidden>
+          <div class="details-inner">
+            <p>That chirping or chattering is usually linked to excitement and predatory focus. Cats may be reacting to movement they want to chase, especially when a window keeps them from acting on the impulse.</p>
+          </div>
+        </div>
+      </div>
+    </section>
+  </main>
+
+  <script>
