  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
  <title>Cat FAQ</title>
  <style>
    :root {
      color-scheme: dark;
      --bg: #0b1020;
      --panel: rgba(17, 24, 39, 0.9);
      --panel-strong: rgba(30, 41, 59, 0.95);
      --border: rgba(148, 163, 184, 0.2);
      --text: #e5eefb;
      --muted: #9fb0c8;
      --accent: #7dd3fc;
      --accent-strong: #38bdf8;
      --shadow: 0 20px 45px rgba(2, 6, 23, 0.45);
    }

    * {
      box-sizing: border-box;
    }

    body {
      margin: 0;
      min-height: 100vh;
      font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;
      background:
        radial-gradient(circle at top, rgba(56, 189, 248, 0.18), transparent 30%),
        linear-gradient(180deg, #020617 0%, var(--bg) 100%);
      color: var(--text);
      display: grid;
      place-items: center;
      padding: 32px 20px;
    }

    .page {
      width: min(820px, 100%);
      background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.72);
      border: 1px solid var(--border);
      border-radius: 24px;
      box-shadow: var(--shadow);
      backdrop-filter: blur(14px);
      overflow: hidden;
    }

    .hero {
      padding: 40px 32px 24px;
      border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
      background: linear-gradient(180deg, rgba(125, 211, 252, 0.08), transparent);
    }

    .eyebrow {
      margin: 0 0 10px;
      font-size: 0.85rem;
      letter-spacing: 0.12em;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      color: var(--accent);
    }

    h1 {
      margin: 0 0 10px;
      font-size: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3rem);
      line-height: 1.1;
    }

    .hero p {
      margin: 0;
      max-width: 60ch;
      color: var(--muted);
      line-height: 1.6;
    }

    .faq {
      padding: 24px;
    }

    .example + .example {
      margin-top: 16px;
    }

    .example {
      background: linear-gradient(180deg, rgba(30, 41, 59, 0.88), rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.96));
      border: 1px solid var(--border);
      border-radius: 18px;
      overflow: hidden;
      transition: transform 180ms ease, border-color 180ms ease, box-shadow 180ms ease;
    }

    .example:hover,
    .example:focus-within {
      transform: translateY(-2px);
      border-color: rgba(125, 211, 252, 0.35);
      box-shadow: 0 14px 30px rgba(2, 6, 23, 0.35);
    }

    .question {
      all: unset;
      display: flex;
      align-items: center;
      justify-content: space-between;
      gap: 16px;
      width: 100%;
      padding: 20px 22px;
      cursor: pointer;
      font-size: 1.05rem;
      font-weight: 700;
      line-height: 1.4;
    }

    .question:focus-visible {
      outline: 2px solid var(--accent);
      outline-offset: -2px;
    }

    .question-text {
      flex: 1;
    }

    .icon {
      width: 34px;
      height: 34px;
      border-radius: 999px;
      display: grid;
      place-items: center;
      flex-shrink: 0;
      color: var(--accent);
      background: rgba(56, 189, 248, 0.1);
      transition: transform 180ms ease, background-color 180ms ease, color 180ms ease;
    }

    .question[aria-expanded="true"] .icon {
      transform: rotate(45deg);
      color: #08111f;
      background: var(--accent-strong);
    }

    .icon::before {
      content: "+";
      font-size: 1.35rem;
      line-height: 1;
    }

    .details {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-rows: 0fr;
      transition: grid-template-rows 220ms ease;
    }

    .details.open {
      grid-template-rows: 1fr;
    }

    .details-inner {
      overflow: hidden;
    }

    .details p {
      margin: 0;
      padding: 0 22px 22px;
      color: var(--muted);
      line-height: 1.7;
    }

    @media (max-width: 640px) {
      .hero {
        padding: 32px 22px 20px;
      }

      .faq {
        padding: 18px;
      }

      .question,
      .details p {
        padding-left: 18px;
        padding-right: 18px;
      }
    }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <main class="page">
    <header class="hero">
      <p class="eyebrow">Frequently asked questions</p>
      <h1>All about cats</h1>
      <p>Explore quick answers about cat behavior, care, and communication. Each question starts collapsed and opens when selected.</p>
    </header>

    <section class="faq" aria-label="Cat FAQ">
      <div class="example">
        <button class="question" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="answer-1">
          <span class="question-text">Why do cats purr?</span>
          <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        </button>
        <div class="details" id="answer-1" hidden>
          <div class="details-inner">
            <p>Cats often purr when they feel safe and content, but they may also purr to comfort themselves when stressed or recovering. It is a flexible sound that can signal both pleasure and self-soothing.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="example">
        <button class="question" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="answer-2">
          <span class="question-text">Why do cats sleep so much?</span>
          <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        </button>
        <div class="details" id="answer-2" hidden>
          <div class="details-inner">
            <p>Cats are natural predators that conserve energy between short bursts of activity. Many adult cats sleep between 12 and 16 hours a day, especially if they live indoors and feel secure.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="example">
        <button class="question" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="answer-3">
          <span class="question-text">Why do cats knead with their paws?</span>
          <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        </button>
        <div class="details" id="answer-3" hidden>
          <div class="details-inner">
            <p>Kneading is a behavior that starts in kittenhood and often carries into adulthood. Cats may knead when they are relaxed, marking a cozy spot with scent glands in their paws or recreating a comforting routine.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="example">
        <button class="question" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="answer-4">
          <span class="question-text">How can I tell if a cat is happy?</span>
          <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        </button>
        <div class="details" id="answer-4" hidden>
          <div class="details-inner">
            <p>Happy cats usually show relaxed body language: soft eyes, a gently upright tail, calm grooming, and interest in play or attention. Slow blinking and choosing to sit near you are also common signs of trust.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="example">
        <button class="question" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="answer-5">
          <span class="question-text">Why do cats chirp at birds or windows?</span>
          <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        </button>
        <div class="details" id="answer-5" hidden>
          <div class="details-inner">
            <p>That chirping or chattering is usually linked to excitement and predatory focus. Cats may be reacting to movement they want to chase, especially when a window keeps them from acting on the impulse.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>

  <script>
    const questions = document.querySelectorAll(".question");

    questions.forEach((button) => {
      button.addEventListener("click", () => {
        const details = document.getElementById(button.getAttribute("aria-controls"));
        const isOpen = button.getAttribute("aria-expanded") === "true";

        button.setAttribute("aria-expanded", String(!isOpen));

        if (isOpen) {
          details.classList.remove("open");
          window.setTimeout(() => {
            if (!details.classList.contains("open")) {
              details.hidden = true;
            }
          }, 220);
          return;
        }

        details.hidden = false;
        requestAnimationFrame(() => {
          details.classList.add("open");
        });
      });
    });
  </script>
</body>
</html>
